    "statement": "For the configuration description M_{g,n}=C^n minus diagonals, an upper bound on W_kH^k(M_{g,n};Q) requires only the lowest-weight surjection W_kH^k(C^n)->>W_kH^k(M_{g,n}), which follows from Deligne's identification of W_k in degree k with the image of any smooth proper compactification, applied to a compactification of C^n. No Gysin exactness for the diagonal divisors, no computation of the kernel of restriction, and no symplectic Schur-Weyl or traceless decomposition of V^{tensor n} is needed for that direction; those are needed only to turn the bound into an isomorphism. Arguments that assert Kunneth summands of H^*(C^n) are summands of R^*f_*Q for f:M_{g,n}->M_g remain invalid, but the surjection route does not make that assertion.",
